license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - intent-based networking
  - large language models
  - QoS provisioning
  - hallucination
  - energy efficiency
  - robustness
abstract: >-
  Code, result tables and documentation for a five-dimensional evaluation of ten lightweight open
  language models (at most 10B parameters, five families) on translating natural-language placement
  intents into service-level objectives (SLOs): translation performance, intent validation,
  hallucination, energy and emissions, and robustness to operator phrasing.
